From: FliperOS <fliperos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ggpo: keep the machines within a frame of each other (FliperOS)

GGPO corrected the drift between two machines only when one was 3 frames
or more ahead, and checked every 240 frames, and Flycast waits one frame
for each correction. Machines whose clocks differ a little (the cabinet's
CRT mode and a PC monitor) settled 4 to 5 frames apart: the one ahead
predicted that many frames of the other's input and saw it about 80 ms
late. Correcting from one frame and checking every 60 frames keeps them 0
to 1 frame apart; the number of one-frame waits is the same (it is the real
difference of the clocks), they just come before the gap grows.
---
diff --git a/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/backends/p2p.cpp b/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/backends/p2p.cpp
index 2283533..59ca55c 100644
--- a/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/backends/p2p.cpp
+++ b/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/backends/p2p.cpp
@@ -9,7 +9,9 @@
 #include <chrono>
 #include <thread>
 
-static const int RECOMMENDATION_INTERVAL           = 240;
+// FliperOS: once a second (GGPO had every 4 s), so a drift of a frame is
+// caught before it grows; each catch is still one frame of wait.
+static const int RECOMMENDATION_INTERVAL           = 60;
 static const int DEFAULT_DISCONNECT_TIMEOUT        = 5000;
 static const int DEFAULT_DISCONNECT_NOTIFY_START   = 750;
 
diff --git a/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/timesync.h b/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/timesync.h
index 83b66d7..7f9217d 100644
--- a/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/timesync.h
+++ b/core/deps/ggpo/lib/ggpo/timesync.h
@@ -13,7 +13,10 @@
 
 #define FRAME_WINDOW_SIZE           40
 #define MIN_UNIQUE_FRAMES           10
-#define MIN_FRAME_ADVANTAGE          3
+// FliperOS: from one frame (GGPO had 3). Machines whose clocks differ a
+// little (a CRT mode and a PC monitor) stayed 3 to 5 frames apart, and the
+// one ahead predicted that many frames of the other's input.
+#define MIN_FRAME_ADVANTAGE          1
 #define MAX_FRAME_ADVANTAGE          9
 
 class TimeSync {
